# Janitza UMG 96RM-E.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Janitza UMG 96RM-E — Modbus register map for Omni Console
# | 
# | Source: janitza-umg96rm-e-modbus.pdf
# | - 3-phase 4-wire power analyzer, DIN-rail, RS485 Modbus RTU.
# | - Holding registers (FC03), IEEE-754 float, big-endian (MSW first, default).
# | - Addresses are 0-based protocol addresses (direct as sent on bus).
# | - All float registers occupy 2 consecutive Modbus registers (32 bits).
# | - Adding 32768 to any address accesses the same value little-endian.
# | - Two register blocks used: "frequently required" at 19000+ and
# | measured values float at 800+.
# | - Factory defaults: slave=1, baud=9600, 8N1.
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Janitza
@model=UMG 96RM-E
@description=3-phase 4-wire power analyzer — per-phase V/I/P/Q/S, CosPhi, PF, Hz, per-phase energy (Wh/VAh/varh), THD; IEEE-754 float holding registers.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/janitza-umg96rm-e.toml; Source: janitza-umg96rm-e-modbus.pdf. Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
